<body>
<h1>Each isolation layer is also a log source - the SIEM is what turns three silent gates into one visible story</h1>

<div class="col root"><div class="row"><div class="card amber"><div class="t">Identity Proxy</div><div class="d">Every request already carries a verified identity (X-App-ID) - log denied auth attempts + which workspace served which request</div>
<div class="d">→ WAF/gateway-style audit log</div></div>
<div class="card"><div class="t">VLAN / ipvlan</div><div class="d">A packet with the wrong VLAN tag trying to reach another tenant's segment is a real signal - an IDS - OSS: Suricata per VLAN; AWS: GuardDuty</div>
<div class="d">→ network-IDS finding, per tenant</div></div>
<div class="card green"><div class="t">gVisor sandbox</div><div class="d">Every syscall the Sentry emulates is visible in-process - an eBPF sensor watching the sandbox catches anomalous syscall - OSS: Falco; AWS: GuardDuty</div>
<div class="d">→ runtime-security finding</div></div></div>
<div class="card"><div class="t">Correlation (the SIEM core)</div><div class="d">same workspace_id / owner attribution across all three sources - 3 unrelated-looking events become 1 incident</div></div>
<div class="arrow">↓</div>
<div class="card"><div class="t">One risk-ranked incident:</div><div class="d">&quot;workspace X - proxy denial, then a VLAN-102 IDS hit, then an anomalous syscall in the same sandbox, within 3 seconds&quot;</div></div></div>
<div class="flowstrip"><div>Identity Proxy &#8594; Correlation (the SIEM core)</div>
<div>VLAN / ipvlan &#8594; Correlation (the SIEM core)</div>
<div>gVisor sandbox &#8594; Correlation (the SIEM core)</div>


</body>
